{% doc %}
  Whether an artist entry is a person or a group, for structured data (DS-164): prints Person or
  Organization. An artist entry can be a collective or a co-operative ("T&T Collective", "West
  Baffin Eskimo Co-operative"), and the entry has no field that says so. Until it has, the
  groups are named in Theme settings, Permanent Collection, one to a line, and matched whole,
  without regard to capitals. Every other artist is a person. Nothing is read from the name
  itself: "Pat and Rosemarie Keough" are two people and "Xwalacktun" is one.

  Capture the output and strip it.

  @param {string} name - The artist's name, as the entry has it

  @example
  {%- capture kind -%}{%- render 'gs-data-artist-kind', name: artist.name.value -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  assign key = name | strip | downcase
  assign groups = settings.artist_groups | downcase | newline_to_br | strip_newlines | split: '<br />'
  assign kind = 'Person'
  for group in groups
    assign group_key = group | strip
    if group_key != blank and group_key == key
      assign kind = 'Organization'
      break
    endif
  endfor
  echo kind
-%}
